  "id": "therapeutic-jurisprudence",
  "term": "therapeutic jurisprudence",
  "definition": "Therapeutic jurisprudence is a framework for thinking about law in terms of its effects on psychological well-being. It holds that legal rules and practices should aim to support mental health and avoid causing harmful psychological consequences.",
